{"type":"text","timestamp":1790453117399,"sessionID":"ses_f20b42e74ffePTBJLmFFTqE4RX","part":{"id":"prt_0df5271bf001j3o6yzbiZYGsd6","messageID":"msg_0df5092b0001kshcTfE07vanL0","sessionID":"ses_f20b42e74ffePTBJLmFFTqE4RX","type":"text","text":"**Maximum steps reached for this agent run — no further tool calls can be made until the next user input.**\n\n## What was accomplished so far (analysis only — **no files have been written yet**)\n\n- **Read all relevant existing files:** `project.godot` (physics layers: 1=World, 2=Player, 3=Enemy, 4=Destructibles, 5=PlayerDamageReceiver, 6=EnemyDamageReceiver, 7=DestructiblesDamageReceiver), `character.gd`/`character.tscn` (base class with `State{IDLE,WALK,ATTACK}`, `DamageEmitter`, `on_emit_damage` emits `damage_received`), `player.tscn` (extends character; idle=frames 0–3, walk=10–17, punch=21–23; body layer=2/mask=9; DamageEmitter mask=96 → layers 6+7), `damage_receiver.gd`/`.tscn`, `damage_emitter.tscn`, `barrel.gd`/`.tscn` (pattern for `damage_received` handling; receiver layer=64), `world.tscn`/`world.gd`.\n- **Analyzed `enemy_boss.png` (480×480, 10×10 grid of 48px frames).** Per-row occupancy/appearance analysis (transparent-pixel counts, bboxes, average colors):\n  - **Row 0** (1 frame): static idle pose frame → **idle = [0]** (start times array of 1 key).\n  - **Row 1** (8 frames): small vertical bobbing cycle → **walk = [10,11,12,13,14,15,16,17]**.\n  - **Row 2/3/4** (4/3/5 frames): attacks (wide arm-extending bboxes) — optional attack resource could use row 2 (frames 20–23).\n  - **Row 5** (2 frames: first is a full-white hit-flash frame, avg 255,255,255; second a recoil pose) → **hurt = [50,51]**. Row 6 (3 frames, bbox falls downward) is knockdown/death. Rows 7 (≈1 valid), 8 (1), 9 (8, alternate run) are less suitable for hurt.\n  - Player sheet suggestion for its **hurt** animation: inspect rows 3/7/8 (each 3 frames); likely `hurt = [30,31,32]` — **needs visual confirmation**.\n\n## Remaining work (all of it)\n\n1. `character.gd`: add `@onready var damage_receiver`, `@export var knockback_intensity`, new `State.HURT`; connect `damage_receiver.damage_received` in `_ready()`; implement `on_receive_damage(damage, direction)` → subtract health, `queue_free()` when health ≤ 0, else set state HURT, play `hurt`, apply knockback `velocity = direction * knockback_intensity`; `can_move()` must exclude HURT; `on_action_complete()` returns to IDLE; likely flip emitter scale is already handled.\n2. `character.tscn`: instance `DamageReceiver` (e.g., `collision_layer`/editable) as a child.\n3. `player.tscn`: add `DamageReceiver` child (`collision_layer=16`, capsule/rect shape around body) and add a 3‑frame `hurt` animation (method-call `on_action_complete` at end), keeping existing idle/walk/punch and movement/attack logic.\n4. `basic_enemy.gd` (extends character.gd): `@export var player : CharacterBody2D`; override `handle_input()` to set velocity chasing `player` (stop when close), optionally trigger ATTACK when within reach; emitter mask should hit layer 5 (PlayerDamageReceiver).\n5. `basic_enemy.tscn`: instance `character.tscn`, script override, texture `enemy_boss.png` (hframes/vframes=10, offset (−24,−48)), body layer=4/mask, DamageEmitter `collision_mask=16`, DamageReceiver `collision_layer=32`, stats (e.g. damage 2–3, health ~12, speed ~25, knockback_intensity), AnimationLibrary with `idle=[0]`, `walk=[10–17]`, `hurt=[50,51] (+on_action_complete)`, RESET, plus an `attack`/punch anim (row 2, frames 20–23) monitoring track optional.\n6. `world.tscn`: add exactly two `BasicEnemy` instances under `ActorsContainer` (e.g. positions (70,38) and (80,55)), each with `player = ExtResource/NodePath(\"Player\")` wired to the existing Player instance.\n7. **Verification:** run `timeout 10 godot --path . --quit-after 2 --write-movie /tmp/opencode/check.png` (GODOT_EXEC_PATH=`/run/gamedevbench-bin/godot`) and screenshot frames to confirm enemies render/chase and no parse errors; check `hurt`/knockback by simulating punches near enemies.\n\n## Recommended next step\n\nOn the next iteration, implement the six file changes above in order (they are independent edits except world.tscn last), then run Godot headless screenshots at multiple timestamps to verify rendering and behavior. The row selections above (idle 0; walk 10–17; hurt 50,51 for boss; player hurt ≈ 30–32 pending a quick look at `player.png` rows 3/7/8) are the key decision points to confirm visually before finalizing.","time":{"start":1790453117375,"end":1790453117378},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"resp_435193a1252c45adb51f81f18b31a18b_msg"}}}}
